{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511659-using-abilities-to-increase-backgrounds","id":1511659,"title":"Using abilities to increase backgrounds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-05-14T15:26:20-07:00","id":1511659,"title":"Using abilities to increase backgrounds","content":"Has anyone thought of (or even devised a system to) using abilities like Commerce, Seneschal, Politics or Finance to make something like rolls to increase backgrounds like Resources and Influence? Perhaps to avoid dealing in-game with the details of money-management, and let investments and regular trade happen during downtime?<br /> <br /> Ex.: roll Intelligence + Commerce / Senschal / Finance (diff. 5 + your current dots in Resources) + any background that could help you (like Influence, Retainers, Contacts or Allies, but losing access to that background for that period for other purposes) every 6 months to attempt increasing your Resources by 1. Botch: lose 1 dot of Resources per each 1 rolled. Failure: no change. Success: increase Resources by 1. 5+ successes: increase Resources by 2 +1 for each 2 successes beyond 5. <br /> <br /> Same with Politics to build up Influence by identifying useful people to have dealings with or bring under your control or support (which also brings them somewhat under your control, depending on the type of support) and then actually doing it, but without gameplaying it because not every such interacion would be interesting (especially if frequent), and it might take too much game time away from other players. Obviously it's good and fun from time to time to play in game how you collect dirt on a political candidate and threaten him or how you blood bind him after getting him to participate in a few meetings of your strange new church, but it can get annoying too if too frequent. And some characters are geared to engage in this regularly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:07:56-07:00","id":1511675,"title":"","content":"I've never used it myself, but I did argue with someone about a game I saw, in particular a scene where the party got stuck in rubble and one of the players who had 3 or 4 dots worth of resources wanted to use them to pay for a jackhammer. to get them out (In this case it would be Charisma or Manipulation + Resources), but the ST asked for a roll with contacts instead of resources, that's because it was 3am in the middle of a graveyard so they would have to do it in an illicit way. Which generated a whole discussion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27832-psicose","name":"Psicose","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27832_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:33:22-07:00","id":1511680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hermeticus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511659-using-abilities-to-increase-backgrounds#post1511659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has anyone thought of (or even devised a system to) using abilities like Commerce, Seneschal, Politics or Finance to make something like rolls to increase backgrounds like Resources and Influence? Perhaps to avoid dealing in-game with the details of money-management, and let investments and regular trade happen during downtime?<br /> <br /> Ex.: roll Intelligence + Commerce / Senschal / Finance (diff. 5 + your current dots in Resources) + any background that could help you (like Influence, Retainers, Contacts or Allies, but losing access to that background for that period for other purposes) every 6 months to attempt increasing your Resources by 1. Botch: lose 1 dot of Resources per each 1 rolled. Failure: no change. Success: increase Resources by 1. 5+ successes: increase Resources by 2 +1 for each 2 successes beyond 5.<br /> <br /> Same with Politics to build up Influence by identifying useful people to have dealings with or bring under your control or support (which also brings them somewhat under your control, depending on the type of support) and then actually doing it, but without gameplaying it because not every such interacion would be interesting (especially if frequent), and it might take too much game time away from other players. Obviously it's good and fun from time to time to play in game how you collect dirt on a political candidate and threaten him or how you blood bind him after getting him to participate in a few meetings of your strange new church, but it can get annoying too if too frequent. And some characters are geared to engage in this regularly.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have, you can contact me and I will be pleased to send you the files","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27429-microcuchon","name":"Microcuchon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"201"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T17:34:51-07:00","id":1511681,"title":"","content":"If you're going to roll to increase Backgrounds, it's probably better to go whole hog and just get rid of a lot of the Backgrounds and make them functions of Ability rolls.<br /> <br /> Rolling to increase Backgrounds just incentivizes investing in Abilities, and putting your Background dots in thing you can't just increase like Generation (even more than that's already the case).<br /> <br /> If you fold Backgrounds into Abilities instead, characters will feel more holistically sensible instead of having a bunch of characters that are just down on their luck temporarily, but will roll to recover their wealth, friendships, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T18:10:48-07:00","id":1511684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1511659-using-abilities-to-increase-backgrounds?p=1511681#post1511681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you're going to roll to increase Backgrounds, it's probably better to go whole hog and just get rid of a lot of the Backgrounds and make them functions of Ability rolls.<br /> <br /> Rolling to increase Backgrounds just incentivizes investing in Abilities, and putting your Background dots in thing you can't just increase like Generation (even more than that's already the case).<br /> <br /> If you fold Backgrounds into Abilities instead, characters will feel more holistically sensible instead of having a bunch of characters that are just down on their luck temporarily, but will roll to recover their wealth, friendships, and so on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I get your point, though, to be honest, I tend to put background dots in Generation anyway usually. The reasoning is that, if I have a social character, I should be capable of acquiring the other backgrounds in the game (if I can't, it means I need to improve my roleplaying skills for social characters). That's just me though, and I'm obviously weird in this.<br /> <br /> I'm also often tempted by the optional rule to purchase backgrounds with xp, Requiem style. Makes their use and acquisition clearer for ST and players and keeps a power balance between smart players who may manage to acquire loads of backgrounds through sheer interpretation and other players who can't get that straight and are limited to what they can buy with xp. And it keeps game time focused on the coterie's adventures as a whole as opposed to individual characters' important but individualistic side-quests (which are not side at all for social characters who depend on and have goals related to their backgrounds).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16965-hermeticus","name":"Hermeticus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"431"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-05-14T18:24:58-07:00","id":1511686,"title":"","content":"That's an option too. Though CofD 2e also kinda does some of what I was talking about.<br /> <br /> In the CofD base rules, items and &quot;services&quot; have an Availability rating. While Allies, Resources, or Status of an appropriate level/type can just get you an invite to a high class party where elites are hobnobbing, a character with high enough Politics can roll to get themselves on the guest list as well. The mechanics of a lot of the CofD Merits that were Backgrounds in the WoD are also a bit more well defined, and generally reward a breadth of traits instead of trying to do everything with just one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}